00:00:17.156 --> 00:00:18.530
One of the most
common challenges

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:19.946
with machine
learning is taking it

00:00:19.946 --> 00:00:22.700
from a large, daunting
process to something that

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.142
actually helps your business.

00:00:24.142 --> 00:00:25.850
If you've ever wrestled
with this problem

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.320
yourself, then good news.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.780
Here's some advice we
give our cloud customers

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.440
as they're getting started.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.200
Maybe you'll find
it useful, too.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.940
Firstly, start simple.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.780
You don't need to build a
self-driving car all at once.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:40.789
Instead, start with
the simplest problems

00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:42.330
you can tackle with
machine learning.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:45.530
In fact, what looks like a
complex application actually

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:48.200
usually starts out as
collections of separate simpler

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.070
components.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:51.560
Secondly, figure out
the business problem

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.850
before you attempt to
figure out machine learning.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.580
You need to have a grasp
of the business impact

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:56.704
your application will have.

00:00:56.704 --> 00:00:58.430
Otherwise, you might
just get caught up

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.650
in the coolness of a
solution to a problem that

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.180
doesn't need any solving.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:05.690
Thirdly, seamlessly integrate
it into applications

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:09.140
as much as possible, because
ultimately, the end user

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:11.600
doesn't care if it works
with machine learning or AI

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:12.680
or whatever.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.510
They look at the functionality.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.240
Fourthly, machine
learning can open you up

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.280
to new user interaction
paradigms that weren't

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:20.850
available to you before.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.690
So don't miss new
opportunities by over-focusing

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:25.550
on old problems.

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:28.670
And finally, even if
it feels daunting,

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:31.370
you should be thinking
big, because AI

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:33.590
is a revolutionary
technology that

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:36.380
will transform all business,
much like the internet

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.630
transformed the world
20, 25 years ago.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:42.680
But remember, you can think
big in bite-sized chunks.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.600
When we work with
customers, we encourage

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:46.210
you to have that big vision.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.740
But we make sure that we work
with you to break it down

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:50.000
into manageable pieces.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.520
And this isn't untested advice.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.330
There's a huge list of
customers that we've

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:55.240
helped achieve success
in machine learning,

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.962
and the talk is densely packed
with many of their stories.

00:01:58.962 --> 00:02:00.920
If it's customer use
cases and practical advice

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.860
you're looking for, do
check out the full talk.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.360
And that's not all
you'll see there.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.910
You'll hear lessons we learned
in becoming an AI company,

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:09.830
and you'll find advice
about the technologies

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.746
that we've built to make
your machine learning

00:02:11.746 --> 00:02:15.170
journey easier, including some
that are hot off the presses.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:18.470
We also take a look at how we're
helping solve the skills gap

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.160
problem in data science.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.490
The world has 21
million developers,

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.740
and of them, only
a few thousand are

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.620
skilled at building
deep learning models.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:28.850
What's to be done about it?

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.050
Find out in the full talk.

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:31.716
And if you like
announcements, this talk

00:02:31.716 --> 00:02:33.020
brings you three big ones.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.450
First, Contact
Center AI; second,

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.700
a new partnership with
Iron Mountain that

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:39.950
lets you use our natural
language understanding

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.020
technologies within
their platform;

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:45.740
and the favorite if you
have a need for speed,

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:48.020
powerful new TPU
hardware in alpha.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.460
And for the cherry
on top, you'll

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.350
see an AutoML demo
where a Frenchman

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.610
teaches you and AI to
recognize soft, round cheeses.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:58.610
And don't be fooled, turns
out they're not all brie.

